<title>EGYPT: Spinalex full-yr profits fall 88 percent.</title>
<headline>Spinalex full-yr profits fall 88 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alexandria Spinning and Weaving (Spinalex) made net attributable profits of 880,000 pounds in the financial year 1995/6, 88 percent down on 7.2 million in the previous year, an official source at the Public Enterprise Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The finanical year ends on June 30.</p>
<p>The profits, which are not audited, are equivalent to 0.46 pounds for each of the 1.926 million shares, which last traded on the Egyptian stock exchange at 21.00 pounds.</p>
<p>The state privatised 96,400 of the shares in 1994.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
